      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Optical-flow frame interpolation from a REAL video (with ground truth)\n\nLoad a clip (the 'Load Video' node lists files in ComfyUI/input - copy images/pedestrian_area.mp4 there, or upload your own). 'Video Slice' keeps a short window so the frame batch stays small; 'Get Video Components' splits it into frames. We pick three CONSECUTIVE frames from the window:\n  frame 0 = A (t=0), frame 2 = B (t=1), and frame 1 = the TRUE middle.\n\nWe interpolate the middle from A and B ONLY (frame 1 is never fed in), then compare to the real frame 1:\n  1. Dense optical flow A->B and B->A (Farneback).\n  2. Warp A forward by t and B backward by 1-t along their flows ('Flow Map' -> cv2.remap); remap samples backward, so the scales are -t and t-1.\n  3. Blend the motion-compensated warps with weights (1-t) and t.\n\nThe two error heatmaps (|interp - real| vs |cross-fade - real|) show the flow result is closer to the true frame than a naive 50/50 blend, which ghosts every moving edge. One knob: the 't' MathExpression (0.5 = middle) drives both warp scales and both blend weights.\n\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
